{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"agent_message","text":"Eight-head grouping is another modest win (local 4096-token timing ≈0.070 ms), and two-wave execution is clearly worse, so one wave stays. I’m now testing a two-stage path for large inputs: compute each token’s trig vector exactly once into a small BF16 scratch tensor, then consume it in the fused Q/K/cache kernel. This adds one launch but removes the remaining 12× trig duplication."}}
